[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    V_{\text{cube}} = s^3
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    where \( s \) is the length of a side. Substituting the given side length:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    V_{\text{cube}} = 4^3 = 64 \text{ cubic feet}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2. **Determine the volume of the cylindrical section removed:**
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    The volume \( V_{\text{cylinder}} \) of a cylinder is given by the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    V_{\text{cylinder}} = \pi r^2 h
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    where \( r \) is the radius and \( h \) is the height. The radius of the cylinder is 2 feet, and the height (or depth) of the cylinder removed is also given as 4 feet. Substituting the given radius and height:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
