[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m We can use the identity for the sum of cubes:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[a^3 + b^3 + c^3 - 3abc = (a + b + c)(a^2 + b^2 + c^2 - ab - bc - ca).\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m We already know \(a + b + c = 0\), so the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[a^3 + b^3 + c^3 - 3abc = 0 \implies a^3 + b^3 + c^3 = 3abc.\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m We also know that \(abc = 17\), so:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[a^3 + b^3 + c^3 = 3 \cdot 17 = 51.\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Therefore, the sum of the cubes of the three numbers is \(\boxed{51}\).<|im_end|>
