[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus, the angle $\theta_k = \frac{\pi}{2} + \frac{\theta}{2}$ or $\theta_k = \frac{\pi}{2} - \frac{\theta}{2}$. For every $k$, the expression $\theta_2 + \theta_4 + \cdots + \theta_{2n}$ is symmetric with respect to flips. To see this, observe that for every $k$, the sum $\theta_2 + \theta_4 + \cdots + \theta_{2n}$ essentially counts symmetrically. We start by noting the periodicity of the terms, finding the sum of phases consistently through modular arithmetic and periodic cycles.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m We calculate:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
