[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m First, we square both sides to eliminate the parentheses and then use trigonometric identities. The left side can be rewritten as:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m (\cos x - 4 \sin x)^2 = 1^2
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Expanding the left side, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
