[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m We know from the Pythagorean identity that \(\cos^2 x + \sin^2 x = 1\). Substituting \(1\) for \(\cos^2 x + \sin^2 x\) in the equation, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 1 - 8 \cos x \sin x + 16 \sin^2 x = 1
