[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Now, we need to find \(\cos 2x = 2 \cos^2 x - 1\). From \(\cos^2 x = \frac{1 - \sin^2 x}{1 + \cos x}\), we can express \(\cos 2x\) in terms of \(\sin 2x\):
