[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To solve for \(\angle CED\), we start by noting that \(O\) is the center of the circle, \(A\) is a point on the circle, \(B\) and \(E\) are points on the circle. The angle \(\angle BAE\) subtended by the minor arc \(BA\) at the center \(O\) is denoted as \(\angle EAO\). Given \(\angle BAE = 43^\circ\), we know that the angle subtended by the same arc at the circumference is half the angle subtended at the center.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
