[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Next, we need to find \(\angle CED\). Since \(\angle EOC\) is the angle subtended by the chord \(OE\) at the circumference, and \(\angle EAO" = 21.5^\circ\), \(\angle ECO\) is an angle in the excentric. When we add the angles \(\angle EAO" = 21.5^\circ\) and \(\angle CED",\) the sum should be a full angle of \(360^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
