[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Since \(25 \equiv 1 \pmod{8}\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m (25)(5)^{-1} = (25)(1) = 25 \cdot 5^{(-1)} = 25 \cdot 5^{-1}.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m We need to find the remainder when 25 is divided by 8. The remainder when 25 is divided by 8 is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 25 = 8 \cdot 3 + 1 \implies 25 \equiv 1 \pmod{8}.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus, the remainder when \((abc + abd + acd + bcd + abcd + abcd)(abcd)^{-1}\) is divided by 8 is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \boxed{1}.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]<|im_end|>
