[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To determine how many whole years it will take for the green technology to recover the costs, we need to calculate the total cost and then divide that by the annual savings in energy bills.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 1. **Calculate the total cost over the lifespan of the technology:**
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - The initial cost is \$10,000.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - The annual maintenance cost is \$650 per year.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - Over the lifespan of the technology (each year), the amount of energy saved each year is \$1200.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    The total annual energy saved is the initial cost plus the annual maintenance cost:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \text{Total energy saved} = 10,000 + 650 = 10,650
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2. **Calculate the number of years needed to recover the initial cost:**
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - The total cost to recover over the lifespan of the technology is the initial cost plus the accumulated cost over the lifespan of the technology.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - The accumulated amount of energy saved over the lifespan of the technology is the total energy saved multiplied by the number of years.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - Let \( n \) be the number of whole years it takes to recover the cost.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - According to the problem, the total cost to recover is the sum of the initial cost and the accumulated energy saved over the lifespan of the technology.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - Therefore, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m      10,000 + 10,650 = 10,650n
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - Simplifying the left side, we get:
