[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find the maximum \( y \)-coordinate of a point on the graph of \( r = \sin 2\theta \), we start by expressing the Cartesian coordinates \((x, y)\) in terms of the polar coordinates \((r, \theta)\). Recall that \( x = r \cos \theta \) and \( y = r \sin \theta \). The given equation \( r = \sin 2\theta \) can be rewritten using the double angle identity for sine: 
