[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find the maximum value of \( y \), we need to determine the maximum value of \( y = 2 \sin^2 \theta \cos \theta \). Let \( k = \cos \theta \) and \( m = \sin \theta \), where \( k^2 + m^2 = 1 \) because \( \cos^2 \theta + \sin^2 \theta = 1 \). Then we have:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ y = 2k^2 \cos \theta \sin \theta = 2k^2 \sin 2\theta. \]
