[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Samson derives utility according the relation  $$\text{Utility} = \text{hours of math done} \times \text{hours of frisbee played}.$$On Monday he plays $t$ hours of frisbee and spends $8 - t$ hours doing math.  On Tuesday, he ends up getting the same amount of utility as Monday while spending $2-t$ hours playing frisbee and $t+3$ hours on math.  Find $t$.  Answer as a fraction in lowest terms.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To determine the value of \( t \), we start by expressing Samson's utility for each day and setting them equal to each other. For Monday, his utility is given by the product of the time spent on math and the time spent playing frisbee:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \text{Utility} = \text{hours of math} \times \text{hours of frisbee} = (8 - t) \times t = 8t - t^2
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m For Tuesday, his utility is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \text{Utility} = \text{hours of math} \times \text{hours of frisbee} = (2 - t) \times (t + 3) = (2 - t)(t + 3)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m According to the problem, the utility on Monday and Tuesday is the same. Therefore, we can set the two expressions equal to each other:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 8t - t^2 = (2 - t)(t + 3)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Next, we expand the right-hand side of the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m (2 - t)(t + 3) = 2t + 6 - t^2 - 3t = -t^2 - t + 6
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m So the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 8t - t^2 = -t^2 - t + 6
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m We can subtract \(-t^2\) from both sides to simplify:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 8t = -t + 6
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Then we add \( t \) to both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 9t = 6
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Solving for \( t \), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m t = \frac{6}{9} = \frac{2}{3}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus, the value of \( t \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \boxed{\frac{2}{3}}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]<|im_end|>
