[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find the probability that all three cards dealt from a standard deck are hearts, we can use the fundamental principle of counting and the classification of suits in a deck. Here is the step-by-step reasoning:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 1. **Total number of cards in the deck:**
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    A standard deck has 52 cards, consisting of 13 clubs, 13 diamonds, 13 hearts, and 13 spades.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2. **Number of ways to choose 3 hearts from hearts:**
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    There are 13 hearts in the deck. The number of ways to choose 3 hearts from 13 is given by the combination formula \(\binom{n}{k} = \frac{n!}{k!(n-k)!}\).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \binom{13}{3} = \frac{13!}{3!(13-3)!} = \frac{13!}{3!10!} = \frac{13 \times 12 \times 11}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 286
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 3. **Total number of ways to choose 3 cards from 52:**
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    Similarly, the number of ways to choose 3 cards from 52 is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \binom{52}{3} = \frac{52!}{3!(52-3)!} = \frac{52!}{3!49!} = \frac{52 \times 51 \times 50}{3 \times 2 \times 1} = 22100
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 4. **Probability calculation:**
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    The probability that all three cards are hearts is the ratio of the number of favorable outcomes (choosing 3 hearts) to the total number of possible outcomes (choosing any 3 cards from the deck):
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    P(\text{all three cards are hearts}) = \frac{\binom{13}{3}}{\binom{52}{3}} = \frac{286}{22100} = \frac{286 \div 286}{22100 \div 286} = \frac{1}{80}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Therefore, the probability that all three cards are hearts is \(\boxed{\frac{1}{80}}\).<|im_end|>
