[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The area of triangle \(GHI\) can be calculated using the determinant formula for the area of a triangle with vertices at \((0,0)\), \((-1 + i - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4})\), \((-1)\), and \((0,0)\):
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ \text{Area of } \triangle GHI = \frac{1}{2} \left| 0(-1 - 0) + (-1 + i - \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4})(0 - 0) + (-1)\left(0 - 0\right) \right| = \frac{1}{2} \left| -1 + \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4} \right| = \frac{1}{2} \left| -1 + \frac{\sqrt{3}}{4} \right|. \]
