[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To determine how many minutes less a 450-mile trip would take compared to a 475-mile trip at an average speed of 50 miles per hour, we can follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 1. **Calculate the time taken for the 450-mile trip:**
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    We know that speed (v) is given by the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    v = \frac{\text{distance}}{\text{time}}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    Rearranging for time (t1), we get:
