[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2. **Condition for a number to be square-free:**
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    A number is square-free if the prime factorization of the number does not include any perfect square. An odd number has only odd prime factors.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 3. **Check each odd integer:**
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    We need to check each odd integer between 3 and 99 to determine if it is square-free.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
