[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - For each number, factorize it to see if it has any perfect squares.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 4. **Use the Kock's theorem (for odd numbers):**
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    There exists a necessary factorization for odd numbers of the form \(a^2 + b \cdot 4\) for \(a > 2\).
