[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find the remainder when \(5^{207}\) is divided by 7, we can use properties of modular arithmetic, specifically the fact that powers of 5 repeat their remainders when divided by 7 as the exponent increases by powers of 4, and repeat every 5 iterations modulo 7 (i.e., \(5^5 \equiv 1 \pmod{7}\)).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m First, we note that \(207 = 36 \times 5 + 9\). Therefore, we need to determine the remainder of \(5^{207}\) when divided by 7 as \(5^9\). Since \(5^4 \equiv 1 \pmod{7}\), we can simplify \(5^9\) using the fact that \(5^4 \equiv 1 \pmod{7}\):
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[5^9 = (5^4)^2 \times 5^2 \equiv 1^2 \times 5^2 \equiv 5^2 \pmod{7}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Now, we calculate \(5^2\):
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[5^2 = 25.\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find the remainder when 25 is divided by 7, we perform the division:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[25 \div 7 = 3 \text{ remainder } 4,\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m so
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[25 \equiv 4 \pmod{7}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Therefore, the remainder when \(5^{207}\) is divided by 7 is \(\boxed{4}\).<|im_end|>
