[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To solve the problem, we start by expressing the integers \(A_n\), \(B_n\), and \(C_n\) in terms of their digits. The integer \(A_n\) is an \(n\)-digit integer with all digits equal to \(a\), so \(A_n = \frac{10^n - 1}{9}\). The integer \(B_n\) is an \(n\)-digit integer with all digits equal to \(b\), so \(B_n = \frac{10^n - 1}{9}\). For the integers \(C_n\) and \(B_n\), and \(A_n\) to satisfy the equation \(C_n - B_n = A_n^2\), we need to find the value of \(a + b + c\).
