[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To verify if this is the largest possible difference, we calculate other possible values and compare them to \(26\). If we use \(a = 4\), \(b = 5\), and \(c = 2\) (since the numbers are one digit from 4 to 6, but now \(c = 2\) would not be a multiple of 3), the numbers in cell (2, top) would be \(3, 2, 4\). The sum would be \(3 + 2 + 4 = 9\), and adding 3 to this would give \(9 + 3 = 12\), which is larger. 
