[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To determine the area of the set \( S \) in the complex plane, we start by interpreting the inequality \( |z - 7 + 10i| \le 5 \). This inequality represents all complex numbers \( z \) that lie within a circle in the complex plane centered at \( 7 - 10i \) with a radius of 5.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The equation \( |z - 7 + 10i| = r \) in Cartesian coordinates can be rewritten as:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ \sqrt{(z - 7)^2 + (z - 10)^2} = r. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m This is a circle with center at \( (7, 10) \) and radius \( r \).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The area \( A \) of a circle is given by the formula \( \pi r^2 \). Here, the radius \( r \) is 5. Therefore, the area of the circle is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ A = \pi \cdot 5^2 = 25\pi. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus, the area of the set \( S \) is \(\boxed{25\pi}\).<|im_end|>
