[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To solve the expression \(\frac{1}{3} - \frac{1}{9} + \frac{1}{27} - \frac{1}{81} + \frac{1}{243}\), we start by recognizing that all the terms in the expression have the same denominators, which is the least common denominator (LCD). The LCD of the denominators 3, 9, 27, 81, and 243 is 243. We can rewrite each fraction with the common denominator 243:
