[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[1\frac{1}{4} = \frac{5}{4}, \quad 3\frac{1}{8} = \frac{25}{8}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Next, rewrite the base exponents with these fractions:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[\left(2^{\frac{5}{4}}\right)^{\frac{2}{5}} \cdot \left(4^{\frac{25}{8}}\right)^{\frac{2}{25}}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Using the property of exponents \((a^m)^n = a^{m \cdot n}\), we can simplify each term:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[\left(2^{\frac{5}{4}}\right)^{\frac{2}{5}} = 2^{\left(\frac{5}{4} \cdot \frac{2}{5}\right)} = 2^{\frac{5 \cdot 2}{4 \cdot 5}} = 2^{\frac{1}{2}} = \sqrt{2},\]
