[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Let \( d \) be the number of positive divisors of \( n^2 \) that are less than \( n \). These divisors are of the form \( 2^a \cdot 3^b \) where \( 0 \leq a \leq 31 \) and \( 0 \leq b \leq 19 \). The total number of divisors of \( n^2 \) is the product of the number of choices for \( a \) and \( b \):
