[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Next, we consider the number of divisors of \( n^2 \) that are prime to \( n \). These divisors are those of the form \( 2^{30} \cdot 3^{19} \) and \( 2^{31} \cdot 3^{18} \). The total number of such divisors is:
