[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Given a real number $x$, let $\lfloor x\rfloor$ denote the greatest integer less than or equal to $x$. For a certain integer $k$, there are exactly 70 positive integers $n_1$, $n_2, \ldots,$ $n_{70}$ such that
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[k = \lfloor \sqrt[3]{n_1} \rfloor = \lfloor \sqrt[3]{n_2} \rfloor =\cdots= \lfloor \sqrt[3]{n_{70}} \rfloor\]and $k$ divides $n_i$ for all $i$ such that $1 \leq i \leq 70$.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Find the maximum value of $\displaystyle\frac{n_i}{k}$ for $1 \leq i \leq 70$.
