[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m First, let's consider the integer part of surds. Since \( k = \lfloor \sqrt[3]{n} \rfloor \), it follows that \( k \leq \sqrt[3]{n} < k+1 \). Therefore, \( k^3 < n < (k+1)^3 \). This means:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m k^3 \leq n \leq (k+1)^3 - 1
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Now, let's calculate the range of \( n \) modulo \( k \). We have:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
