[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m This means that \( n \) can be written as \( n = mk - 1 \) for some integer \( m \). For \( n \) to satisfy \( k \) divides \( n \), \( n \) must be a multiple of \( k \), i.e., \( n = k \tau \) for some integer \( \tau \), where \( k \) is a multiple of \( k \).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The number of such \( n \) is the number of multiples of \( k \) between \(-k\) and \(k\), inclusive. This is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
