[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find the area of the largest possible inscribed triangle having one side as a diameter of circle \( C \), we start by noting that a diameter of circle \( C \) is twice the radius. Therefore, a diameter of circle \( C \) is \( 2 \times 6 = 12 \) cm.
