[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The inscribed triangle will be an isosceles triangle with its base along the diameter of the circle, sharing its base with the other two sides of the triangle, which are equal (since the diameter is the longest possible inscribed object that can fit with the triangle formed). The height of this isosceles triangle will be the radius of the inscribed circle, \( r = 6 \) cm.
