[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m First, let's denote the total number of games played by all teams as \(35\) (since each of the \(7\) teams plays every other team exactly once). When team \(A\) wins \(A - B\) games, the number of games won by team \(B\) is \(35 - (A - B)\). Team \(B\) wins \(35 - (B - A)\) games. Team \(A\) wins \(A - B\) games, and team \(B\) wins \(B - A\) games, along with a 50% chance of winning the game they played.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Let's define the random variable \(X\) as the number of games team \(A\) wins. Since team \(A\) has already won \(A - B\) games and team \(B\) has already won \(B - A\) games, the number of games team \(A\) wins can be either:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 1. \(A - B\),
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2. \(B - A\),
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m or 0 if and only if team \(B\) also wins exactly \( B - A \) games.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The probability of winning exactly \(k\) games out of \(35\) is given by the binomial distribution:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m P(X = k) = \binom{35}{k}(0.5)^{35}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The probability of winning \(A - B\) games is the number of ways to choose \(A - B\) penalties for team \(A\) and the remaining \(35 - (A - B)\) penalties for team \(B\):
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m P(X = A - B) = \sum_{k = A - B}^{35} \binom{35}{k} (0.5)^{35}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m We need to find the probability that team \(A\) finishes with more points than team \(B\):
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m P(A > B) = 1 - P(A = B)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The probability \(P(A = B)\) is the sum of the probabilities of team \(A\) winning all games:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m P(A = B) = \sum_{k = 1}^{\infty} P(X = k)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m For even \(A - B\):
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m P(A = B) = \sum_{k = 0}^{\infty} \left( \binom{35}{k} (0.5)^{35} \right)^2 \left( \binom{35 - (A - B)}{35 - (A - B)} (0.5)^{35 - (A - B)}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m For odd \(A - B\):
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m P(A = B) = 0
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The probability \(P(A > B)\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m P(A > B) = 1 - P(A = B) = 1 - 0 = 1
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The probability that team \(A\) finishes with more points than team \(B\) is:
