[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find the volume of the region given by the inequality \( |x + y + z| + |x + y - z| + |x - y + z| + |-x + y + z| \le 4 \), we start by analyzing the expression on the left-hand side. Since the expression is symmetric in \(x, y, z\), we can consider different cases based on the signs of \(x + y - z\), \(x - y + z\), and \(-x + y + z\).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m ### Case 1: \(x + y - z \ge 0\)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m In this case, all expressions simplify to \(x + y + z\), so the inequality becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ (x + y + z) + (x + y - z) + (x - y + z) + (-x + y + z) \le 4. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Simplifying, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ 3x + 2z \le 4. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m ### Case 2: \(x + y - z \le 0\)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m In this case, all expressions simplify to \(x - y + z\), so the inequality becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ (x - y + z) + (x + y - z) + (x - y + z) + (-x + y + z) \le 4. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Simplifying, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ 2x + 2z \le 4, \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ x + z \le 2. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m ### Case 3: \(x - y + z \ge 0\)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m In this case, all expressions simplify to \(-x + y + z\), so the inequality becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ (-x + y + z) + (-x + y + z) + (x - y + z) + (-x + y + z) \le 4. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Simplifying, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ -x + 4z \le 4, \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ -x + 4 + 4z \le 4. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m This is always false. Similarly, in the case \(x - y + z \le 0\) and \(-x + y + z \ge 0\), we get counter obvious contradictions because:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ -x + y + z + (-x + y + z) + (x - y + z) \le 4. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m ### Case 4: \(x - y + z \le -x + y + z\)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m In this case, we simplify to:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ (x - y + z) + (-x + y + z) + (-x + y + z) + (x - y + z) \le 4. \]
