[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To compute \(\left\lfloor \frac{2007! + 2004!}{2006! + 2005!} \right\rfloor\), we start by simplifying the fraction inside the floor function. We use the factorial identity \(2x! = (x+1)(x!) - 1\) to rewrite \(2007! + 2004!\) in a more manageable form.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m First, express \(2007!\) and \(2004!\) in terms of \(2005!\):
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2007! = 2007 \cdot 2006 \cdot 2005! = (2007 \cdot 2006) \cdot 2005! = (2006 + 1)(2006 + 2) \cdot 2005! = (2006 + 1)(2006 + 2)(2005!) + 9 \cdot 2005!.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2004! = 2004 \cdot 2003!,
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m and thus,
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2007! + 2004! = (2006 + 1)(2006 + 2)(2005!) + 9 \cdot 2005! + 2004! = (2007 \cdot 2006 \cdot 2005! + 1) + 9 \cdot 2005! + 2004!.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m We can rewrite \(2006 + 1\) as \(2006 \cdot 2005 + 1\), and the above expression simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2007! + 2004! = (2007 \cdot 2006 \cdot 2005! + 1 + 9 \cdot 2005! + 2004!) = (2007 \cdot 2006 \cdot 2005! + 8 \cdot 2005! + 1) + 1 = (2007 \cdot 2006 \cdot 2005! + 8 \cdot 2005! + 1) + 1.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m This expression is not easily simplified into a form that is directly useful in simplifying the original problem. Instead, we directly compute the fraction:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \frac{2007! + 2004!}{2006! + 2005!} = \frac{2007 \cdot 2006 \cdot 2005! + 1}{2006 \cdot 2005! + 8 \cdot 2005! + 1} = \frac{2006 \cdot 2005! + 1}{2006 \cdot 2005! + 8 \cdot 2005! + 1} = \frac{2006 \cdot 1 + 1}{2006 \cdot 1 + 8 \cdot 1 + 1} = \frac{2006 + 1}{2006 + 8 + 1} = \frac{2007}{2013}.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus, we need to compute \(\left\lfloor \frac{2007}{2013} \right\rfloor = \left\lfloor \frac{2007}{2013} \cdot 1 \right\rfloor = \left\lfloor \frac{2007}{1} \cdot \frac{1}{1} \right\rfloor = \left\lfloor 2007 \right\rfloor = 2007\).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \boxed{2007}.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]<|im_end|>
