[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To compute the value of \[\cos^6 0^\circ + \cos^6 1^\circ + \cos^6 2^\circ + \dots + \cos^6 90^\circ,\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m we can use the trigonometric identity \(\cos^2 x = \frac{1 + \cos 2x}{2}\) to express \(\cos^6 x\) in terms of \(\cos 2x\). The identity gives us:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[\cos^6 x = \left(\frac{1 + \cos 2x}{2}\right)^2 = \frac{1 + 2\cos 2x + \cos^2 2x}{4}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus,
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[\cos^6 x = \frac{1 + 2\cos 2x + \frac{1 + \cos 2x}{2}}{4} = \frac{1 + 2\cos 2x + \frac{1}{2} + \frac{\cos 2x}{2}}{4} = \frac{3/2 + \cos 2x + \frac{\cos 2x}{2}}{4} = \frac{3/2 + \frac{3}{2} \cos 2x}{4} = \frac{3}{8} (1 + \cos 4x).\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m However, for our specific problem, we only need \(\cos^6 2^\circ + \cos^6 6^\circ\). Using the earlier trigonometric identity, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[\cos 2x = \cos (20^\circ) = \cos (40^\circ - 30^\circ) = \cos 40^\circ \cos 30^\circ + \sin 40^\circ \sin 30^\circ = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \cos 40^\circ + \frac{1}{2} \sin 40^\circ = \frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \cos 40^\circ + \frac{1}{2} \sin 40^\circ.\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus,
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[\cos^6 2^\circ = \left(\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \cos 40^\circ + \frac{1}{2} \sin 40^\circ\right)^6 = \frac{(\sqrt{3})^6}{2^6} \cos^6 40^\circ + 3 (\frac{1}{2})^6 \sin^6 40^\circ = \frac{27}{64} \cos^6 40^\circ + \frac{3}{6400} \sin^6 40^\circ.\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Summing this from \(0^\circ\) to \(90^\circ\), we get
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[\sum_{x=0}^{90} \cos^6 2x = \frac{27}{64} \sum_{l=0}^{29} \sum_{n=l+1}^{40} \cos^{6} l^\circ = \frac{27}{64} \cdot 2 \sum_{l=0}^{29} \left(\frac{\sqrt{3}}{2} \cos 40^\circ + \frac{1}{2} \sin 40^\circ\right)^{12} = \frac{135}{64} \cdot 2 \cos^6 40^\circ.\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m We use the known result:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[\cos^6 x = \frac{105 + 60 \sin 20x}{4376}\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m and integrate term by term from \(0^\circ\) to \(90^\circ\):
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[\sum_{x=0}^{90} \cos^6 2x = \frac{105}{2048} + \frac{60 \cdot 45^\circ}{2 \cdot 2048} = \frac{105}{2048} + \frac{975}{2048} = \frac{1090}{2048} = \frac{27}{512}.\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus, the value of the given sum is \(\boxed{\frac{27}{512}}\).<|im_end|>
