[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To determine the remainder when \(9^{1995}\) is divided by 7, we start by simplifying \(9 \mod 7\). Since \(9 \equiv 2 \pmod{7}\), we can rewrite the problem as finding \(2^{1995} \mod 7\).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m First, we observe the pattern in the powers of 2 modulo 7:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2^1 \equiv 2 \pmod{7}
