[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m This tells us that the powers of 2 repeat every 3 terms modulo 7: \(2^1 \equiv 2\), \(2^2 \equiv 4\), \(2^3 \equiv 1\). Therefore, we can express \(2^n\) in terms of these repeats:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2^n \equiv 2^{n \mod 3} \pmod{7}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find \(2^{1995} \mod 7\), we need to determine \(1995 \mod 3\):
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
