[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find the complex number \( z \) that satisfies the equation \( 2z - 3i\bar{z} = -7 + 3i \), we start by expressing \( z \) in terms of its real and imaginary parts. If \( z = x + yi \), then the conjugate reciprocal is \( \bar{z} = x - yi \).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Given the equation:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ 2z - 3i\bar{z} = -7 + 3i, \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m we substitute \( z = x + yi \) and \( \bar{z} = x - yi \):
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ 2(x + yi) - 3i(x - yi) = -7 + 3i. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Expanding and simplifying the left side, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ 2x + 2yi - 3ix + 3yi^2 = -7 + 3i, \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m which is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ 2x - 3x + y(2 + 3i) = -7 + 3i, \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m or
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ -x + 3y + yi = -7 + 3i. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m By comparing the real and imaginary parts on both sides, we have the system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ -x + 3y = -7, \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ x = 3. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Substituting \( x = 3 \) into the first equation, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ -3 + 3y = -7, \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m or
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ 3y = -4, \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m so
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ y = -\frac{4}{3}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Therefore, the complex number \( z \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ z = 3 - \frac{4}{3}i. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Expressing this in the standard form \( re^{i\theta} \), we note that \( r = \sqrt{3^2 + \left(-\frac{4}{3}\right)^2} = \sqrt{9 + \frac{16}{9}} = \sqrt{\frac{81}{9} + \frac{16}{9}} = \sqrt{\frac{97}{9}} = \frac{\sqrt{97}}{3} \), and \( \theta = -\arg\left(3 - \frac{4}{3}i\right) \).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find \( \theta \), we compute the argument of \( 3 - \frac{4}{3}i \). The argument of \( 3 - \frac{4}{3}i \) is the angle whose sine is 3 and whose cosine is \(-\frac{4}{3}\). The reference angle is \( \tan^{-1}\left(\frac{3}{-4}\right) = -\tan^{-1}\left(\frac{3}{4}\right) \). Since we are in the fourth quadrant, we use an equivalent angle that is \( \pi - (-\tan^{-1}\left(\frac{3}{4}\right)) = \pi + \tan^{-1}\left(\frac{3}{4}\right) \). Importantly, \( \theta = -\left(\tan^{-1}\left(\frac{3}{4}\right) + \frac{\pi}{2}\right) = \frac{\pi}{2} - \tan^{-1}\left(\frac{3}{4}\right) \).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus, the complex number \( z \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ \boxed{3 - \frac{4}{3}i}. \]<|im_end|>
