[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \frac{3}{7} < \frac{M}{56} < \frac{1}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Next, we solve for \( M \) by multiplying all parts of the inequality by 56:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 56 \cdot \frac{3}{7} < M < 56 \cdot \frac{1}{4}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Simplifying the fractions:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 24 < M < 14
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The integer values of \( M \) that satisfy this inequality are:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 25, 26, 27, 28, 29, 30
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m There are 6 integer values of \( M \) that satisfy the inequality. To find the average of these values, we sum them up:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 25 + 26 + 27 + 28 + 29 + 30 = 165
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The average of these integers is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \frac{165}{6} = \frac{55}{2} = 27.5
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus, the average of all integer values of \( M \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \boxed{27.5}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]<|im_end|>
