[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m We observe that the powers of \(i\) repeat every 4 terms: \(i, -1, -i, 1\). This means that for any integers \(x\) and \(y\), \(i^x\) and \(i^y\) either both have the same or opposite signs, and therefore \(i^x + i^y\) will be real if and only if \(i^{x+y}\) is the same (or opposite) of both \(i^x\) and \(i^y\).
