[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find the area of a triangle given its vertices \((x_1, y_1)\), \((x_2, y_2)\), and \((x_3, y_3)\) in a Cartesian coordinate plane, we use the following formula:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left| x_1(y_2 - y_3) + x_2(y_3 - y_1) + x_3(y_1 - y_2) \right|
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m For the given vertices \((5, -2)\), \((10, 5)\), and \((5, 5)\), we substitute these coordinates into the formula:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left| 5(5 - 5) + 10(5 - (-2)) + 5(-2 - 5) \right|
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Simplify the expression inside the absolute value:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \left| 5(0) + 10(7) + 5(-7) \right| = \frac{1}{2} \left| 0 + 70 - 35 \right| = \frac{1}{2} \left| 35 \right|
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Since the absolute value is always non-negative, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \text{Area} = \frac{1}{2} \times 35 = \frac{35}{2} = 17.5
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus, the area of the triangle is \(\boxed{17.5}\) square units.<|im_end|>
