[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find the sum of the squares of the roots of the polynomial equation \(x^{2018} + 44x^{2015} + 3x^3 + 404 = 0\), we start by letting the roots be \(r_1, r_2, \ldots, r_{2018}\). By Vieta's formulas, we know:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 1. The sum of the roots \(r_1 + r_2 + \cdots + r_{2018} = -\frac{44}{1} = -44\).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2. The sum of the product of the roots taken two at a time \(r_1r_2 + r_1r_3 + \cdots + r_{2017}r_{2018} = \frac{3}{1} = 3\).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 3. The sum of the product of the roots \(r_1r_2\cdots r_{2018} = -\frac{404}{1} = -404\).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m We need to find the sum of the squares of the roots, \(r_1^2 + r_2^2 + \cdots + r_{2018}^2\). We can use the identity:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[r_1^2 + r_2^2 + \cdots + r_{2018}^2 = (r_1 + r_2 + \cdots + r_{2018})^2 - 2 \left(\sum_{\text{indiv. terms}} r_i^2\right).\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The first term is the square of the sum of the roots:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[(r_1 + r_2 + \cdots + r_{2018})^2 = (-44)^2 = 1936.\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Now we need to find \(\sum_{\text{indiv. terms}} r_i^2\). Observe that:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[r_1^2 + r_2^2 + \cdots + r_{2018}^2 = (r_1 + r_2 + \cdots + r_{2018})^2 - 2 \left(\sum_{\text{all terms}} r_i^2\right) - 2 \left(\sum_{\text{all terms}} r_i^2\right) + \sum_{\text{indiv. terms}} r_i^2.\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The third and fourth terms in the expansion of \((r_1 + r_2 + \cdots + r_{2018})^2\) are \(-\frac{44}{4} = -44\) and \(\frac{404}{4} = 101\), respectively. So we have:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[r_1^2 + r_2^2 + \cdots + r_{2018}^2 = 1936 - 2 \left(-44 - 101\right) = 1936 - 2 \cdot 145 = 1936 - 290 = 1646.\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus, the sum of the squares of the roots is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[\sqrt{1646^2 - 2 \left(4529\right)} = \sqrt{2691316 - 9058} = \sqrt{2682258} = 5178.\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Therefore, the sum of the squares of the roots is \(\boxed{5178}\).<|im_end|>
