[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m A railroad trestle spans a gorge 80 feet wide and connects two cliffs at heights of 112 and 172 feet above the bottom of the gorge. A train is crossing this gorge from the higher cliff to the lower. When the front of the train has traveled $\frac{3}{4}$ of the trestle's length, how many feet is it above the bottom of the gorge?
