[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m We can factor out the constants from the sum on the left-hand side:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[1987 \cdot 1 + 1987 \cdot 2 + 1987 \cdot 3 + \dots + 1987 \cdot 1986 + 1987 \cdot 1987.\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Now, we can factor out the constant 1987 from each term:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[1987 (1 + 2 + 3 + \dots + 1986 + 1987).\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The sum inside the parentheses is the sum of the first 1987 positive integers, which is given by the formula for the sum of an arithmetic series:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[1 + 2 + 3 + \dots + 1986 + 1987 = \frac{1987 \cdot 1988}{2} = 1987 \cdot 994.\]
