[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 1. Check if 1391 is divisible by 2: Since 1391 is odd, it is not divisible by 2.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2. Check if 1391 is divisible by 3: The sum of the digits of 1391 is \(1 + 3 + 9 + 1 = 14\), and since 14 is not divisible by 3, 1391 is not divisible by 3.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 3. Check if 1391 is divisible by 5: Since 1391 does not end in 0 or 5, it is not divisible by 5.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 4. Check if 1391 is divisible by 7: Perform the division \(1391 \div 7 = 198.7142857\), which is not an integer, so 1391 is not divisible by 7.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 5. Check if 1391 is divisible by 11: The alternating sum of the digits of 1391 is \(1 - 3 + 9 - 1 = 6\), and since 6 is not divisible by 11, 1391 is not divisible by 11.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 6. Check if 1391 is divisible by 13: Perform the division \(1391 \div 13 = 108.6923077\), which is not an integer, so 1391 is not divisible by 13.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 7. Check if 1391 is divisible by 17: Perform the division \(1391 \div 17 = 82.3529412\), which is not an integer, so 1391 is not divisible by 17.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 8. Check if 1391 is divisible by 19: Perform the division \(1391 \div 19 = 72.1052632\), which is not an integer, so 1391 is not divisible by 19.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 9. Check if 1391 is divisible by 23: Perform the division \(1391 \div 23 = 59\), and since 59 is an integer, 1391 is divisible by 23.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus, the prime factorization of 1391 is \(1391 = 23 \times 59\). The largest prime factor of 1391 is 59.
