[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Given that the radius of the inscribed circle (inradius) is 6 cm, we can find the length of \( OA \) using the formula for the inradius of a right triangle:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m r = \frac{a + b - c}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m where \( a \) and \( b \) are the legs of the right triangle, and \( c \) is the hypotenuse. For our triangle, \( a = AB \), \( b = AO = 6 \), and \( c = OB \).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
