[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To solve the problem, we need to determine the value of \( x \), the number of pieces in each complete pack of cherry gum, given the conditions described.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m First, let's define the variables and understand the relationships:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m - Chewbacca starts with 20 pieces of cherry gum and 30 pieces of grape gum.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m - Let \( x \) be the number of pieces in each complete pack.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m - If Chewbacca loses one pack of cherry gum, the number of cherry gum pieces he has becomes \( 20 - x \). The number of grape gum pieces he has remains 30.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m - If he finds 5 packs of grape gum, he gets \( 5 \times x = 5x \) pieces of grape gum. The number of cherry gum pieces he has becomes \( 20 - x \). The number of grape gum pieces he has remains 30.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m According to the problem, the ratio of the number of cherry gum pieces he has to the number of grape gum pieces he has after losing the incomplete pack of cherry gum is the same as the ratio of the number of cherry gum pieces he has to the number of grape gum pieces he has after finding 5 packs of grape gum. This can be expressed as:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \frac{20 - x}{30} = \frac{20 - x}{5x}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To solve this equation, we can eliminate the fractions by multiplying both sides by \( 15x \):
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 5(20 - x) = 3(30)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 100 - 5x = 90
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Subtract 90 from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 10 - 5x = 0
