[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Subtract 10 from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m -5x = -10
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Divide both sides by -5:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m x = 2
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus, the number of pieces in each complete pack is \(\boxed{2}\).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To verify, let's check the solution:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m - If Chewbacca loses one pack of cherry gum, he has \( 20 - 2 = 18 \) pieces of cherry gum and 30 pieces of grape gum.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m - If he finds 5 packs of grape gum, he gets \( 5 \times 2 = 10 \) pieces of grape gum. He has \( 18 - 10 = 8 \) pieces of cherry gum and 30 pieces of grape gum.
