[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To determine the greatest possible value of \( x \) such that the least common multiple (LCM) of \( x \), \( 10 \), and \( 14 \) is \( 70 \), we start by recalling the relationship between the greatest common divisor (GCD) and the LCM of two numbers. The LCM of two numbers \( a \) and \( b \) is given by \( \frac{|a \cdot b|}{\text{GCD}(a, b)} \). Therefore, the LCM of \( x \), \( 10 \), and \( 14 \) is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
