[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2. If \( d = 2 \), then \( x - 7 = 2 \) implies \( x = 9 \).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 3. If \( d = 5 \), then \( x - 7 = 5 \) implies \( x = 12 \).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The greatest possible value of \( x \) that satisfies all conditions is the largest of the values obtained from the possible values of \( d \), which is 9. This value is \( x = 9 \).
