[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find the number of square units in the sum of the areas of the two squares \(ABCD\) and \(AEFG\), we start by noting that angles \(EAB\) and \(ECD\) are right angles. Let the side length of the larger square \(ABCD\) be \(x\). Since \(ABCD\) and \(AEFG\) are squares, the side length of the smaller square \(AEFG\) is \(x\sqrt{2}\).
