[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To determine how many positive four-digit integers of the form \_\_45 are divisible by 45, we need to establish the conditions under which a number of this form is divisible by 45. A number is divisible by 45 if and only if it is divisible by both 9 and 5.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 1. **Divisibility by 9**: A number is divisible by 9 if the sum of its digits is divisible by 9. Since the number ends in 45, it is divisible by 5 (the last digit is 5), and the sum of its digits is composed of the digits 4 and 5. Therefore, the number is divisible by 9 if the number of digits ending in 4 is at most 2 (so they contribute only 4) and the sum of the digits ending in 4 is 9, which is divisible by 9.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2. **Divisibility by 5**: A number is divisible by 5 if its last digit is either 0 or 5.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Since the number ends in 45, it will be divisible by 9 but it will be at least 5 times its first digit (4). Therefore, the possible numbers are those between 450 and 459, inclusive. This means there are 56 numbers that match our criteria (59 - 4 + 1 = 56).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus, the number of positive four-digit integers of the form \_\_45 that are divisible by 45 is \(\boxed{56}\).<|im_end|>
