[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find the values of \(a\) and \(c\) given the cross product of the vectors \(\begin{pmatrix} a \\ -1 \\ c \end{pmatrix}\) and \(\begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ 3 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix}\) is \(\begin{pmatrix} -11 \\ -16 \\ 25 \end{pmatrix}\), we start by writing the equation for the cross product:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \begin{pmatrix} a \\ -1 \\ c \end{pmatrix} \times \begin{pmatrix} 7 \\ 3 \\ 5 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} a \cdot 5 - (-1) \cdot 3 \\ -1 \cdot 7 - c \cdot 5 \\ c \cdot 3 - (-1) \cdot 7 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 5a - 3 \\ -7 - 5c \\ 3c + 7 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} -11 \\ -16 \\ 25 \end{pmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m This gives us the following system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \begin{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 5a - 3 = -11, \\
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m -7 - 5c = -16, \\
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 3c + 7 = 25.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \end{cases}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m We solve each equation step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m First, solve the first equation:
