[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To determine how many positive even perfect cubes are less than 2008, we first identify the range of even perfect cubes that are less than 2008. The smallest even perfect cube is \(2^3 = 8\), and the largest even perfect cube less than 2008 is \(64^3 = 2^{12}\). However, \(64^3 = 2^{12} \cdot 64\), which is not less than 2008. Instead, \(4^3 = 64\) is the largest odd perfect cube.
