[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Using the logarithm property \(\log_b(xy) = \log_b x + \log_b y\), we can rewrite each equation as:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \log_{10} (ALM) = 2, \\
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \log_{10} (MLR) = 3, \\
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \log_{10} (RARL) = 4.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Let \(x = \log_{10} (ALM),\) \(y = \log_{10} (MLR),\) and \(z = \log_{10} (RARL).\) Then we have:
