[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The digit set is {1, 2, 3, 4, 5}. We have three odd digits (1, 3, 5) and two even digits (2, 4).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 1. For every odd digit, it must appear in every even-odd position. This means that each odd digit will appear in exactly half of the 5 slots between the odd digits.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2. The number of odd digits in the set {1, 3, 5} is 3 (since three out of five are odd), so for each of these 3 odd digits, there are 2 choices (either odd-position or even-position).
