[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Let $a_1, a_2, \ldots, a_{2005}$ be real numbers such that $$\begin{array}{ccccccccccc}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m a_1\cdot 1 &+ &a_2 \cdot 2 &+& a_3 \cdot 3 &+ &\cdots& + &a_{2005} \cdot 2005 &=& 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m a_1\cdot 1^2 &+& a_2\cdot 2^2 &+& a_3 \cdot 3^2 &+ &\cdots& + & a_{2005} \cdot 2005^2 &=& 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m a_1 \cdot 1^3 &+& a_2 \cdot 2^3 &+& a_3 \cdot 3^3 &+ &\cdots& + & a_{2005} \cdot 2005^3 &=& 0 \\ \vdots&&\vdots&&\vdots&&&&\vdots&&\vdots \\
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m a_1\cdot 1^{2004} &+& a_2\cdot 2^{2004} &+& a_3\cdot 3^{2004} &+ &\cdots& + &a_{2005} \cdot 2005^{2004} &=& 0
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \end{array}$$and $$\begin{array}{ccccccccccc}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m a_1 \cdot 1^{2005}& +& a_2\cdot 2^{2005} &+& a_3\cdot 3^{2005} &+ &\cdots& + &a_{2005} \cdot 2005^{2005} &=& 1.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \end{array}$$What is the value of $a_1$?
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 1. We are given the following system of equations:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \begin{array}{ccccccccccc}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    a_1 \cdot 1 + a_2 \cdot 2 + a_3 \cdot 3 + \cdots + a_{2005} \cdot 2005 &=& 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    a_1 \cdot 1^2 + a_2 \cdot 2^2 + a_3 \cdot 3^2 + \cdots + a_{2005} \cdot 2005^2 &=& 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    &\vdots& \vdots \\
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    a_1 \cdot 1^{2004} + a_2 \cdot 2^{2004} + a_3 \cdot 3^{2004} + \cdots + a_{2005} \cdot 2005^{2004} &=& 0
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2. To solve this system, let \( a_i = b_i \) if \( i \) is odd and \( a_i = a_i \) if \( i \) is even. Then the equations become:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \begin{array}{ccccccccccc}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    b_1 + 2b_2 + 3b_3 + \cdots + 2005b_{2005} &=& 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    b_1 + 4b_2 + 9b_3 + \cdots + 2005b_{2005}^2 &=& 0 \\
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    &\vdots& \vdots \\
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    b_1 + 16b_2 + 25b_3 + \cdots + 2005b_{2005}^{2004} &=& 1
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \end{array}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 3. Notice that each term is of the form \( \sum_{i=1}^{2005} (bi)^{k_i} \) where \( k_i = i \) if \( i \) is odd and \( k_i = -i \) if \( i \) is even. Therefore, each sum on the right side is the sum of the series modulo 2.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 4. Let \( S(x) = \sum_{i=1}^{2005} x^{k_i} \). We know from the last equation that:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    x^{k_j} \equiv -x^{k_j-1} \pmod{2} \quad \text{for } j = 1, 2, \ldots, 2005.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    This implies that the exponent of \( x \) in a binomial expansion modulo 2 is 0, meaning each odd power \( x^{2005} \equiv x^1 \equiv 1 \pmod{2} \). Therefore, the equation \( S(x) \equiv 1 \pmod{2} \) holds modulo 2.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 5. Since \( S(x) \) has the property that every even power of \( x \) equals 0 modulo 2, and all odd powers are congruent to 1 modulo 2, we must have:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    S(0) \equiv 0 \pmod{2}.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 6. Therefore, the sum \( S(1) + S(1+2) + \cdots + S(2005) \) must equal 0 modulo 2. Notice that each pair \((1, 2), (1+2, 2+2), \ldots, (1+999, 2005+2005)\) contains two terms of the form \( x^{733} \equiv -x^{2} \pmod{2} \), ensuring that \( S(1) + S(2) + \cdots + S(2005) \equiv 0 \pmod{2} \).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 7. Given that:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    S(1) = \frac{1-(-1)^{2005}}{1-i}(1+1) = 0,
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    by the geometric series sum formula, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    S(1) + S(2) + \cdots + S(2005) = \frac{1}{2} \times 0 = 0.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 8. Thus, the value of \( a_1 \) must be:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \boxed{\frac{1}{3}}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m [Ground Truth]
