[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m A star-polygon is drawn on a clock face by drawing a chord from each number to the fifth number counted clockwise from that number.  That is, chords are drawn from 12 to 5, from 5 to 10, from 10 to 3, and so on, ending back at 12.  What is the degree measure of the angle at each vertex in the star-polygon?
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Please reason step by step, and put your final answer within \boxed{{}}.<|im_end|>
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To determine the degree measure of the angle at each vertex in the star-polygon, we start by identifying the sides of the polygon and the angles formed by connecting them and the vertices of the star.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The star-polygon is formed by drawing chords from each number to the fifth number counted clockwise and then drawing chords adjacent to these lines. The degrees of the angles at each vertex of the polygon correspond to the measures of the arcs subtended by the chord lengths.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The chords are drawn as follows:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m - From 12 to 5
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m - From 5 to 10
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m - From 10 to 3
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m - From 3 to 6
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m - From 6 to 9
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m - From 9 to 12 (This is just a count of the numbers)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The sum of the measures of the arcs subtended by these chords is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[360^\circ \times 5 = 1800^\circ\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m This is because each number is an arc of 360 degrees, and there are 5 such arcs for each vertex (12, 5, 10, 3, 6).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Since a star polygon has 5 vertices, and each vertex subtends an arc that is one-third of the total sum of the arcs, the measure of each arc (and thus the measure of each angle) is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[\frac{1800^\circ}{5} = 360^\circ\]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Therefore, the measure of each angle at each vertex of the star-polygon is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[\boxed{36}\]<|im_end|>
