[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \text{det} = a_{11} \begin{vmatrix} 5 & -1 \\ -2 & 1 \end{vmatrix} - a_{12} \begin{vmatrix} 0 & -1 \\ 4 & 1 \end{vmatrix} + a_{13} \begin{vmatrix} 0 & 5 \\ 4 & -2 \end{vmatrix}.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m First, we calculate each of the 2x2 determinants:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \begin{vmatrix} 5 & -1 \\ -2 & 1 \end{vmatrix} = (5 \cdot 1) - (-1 \cdot -2) = 5 - 2 = 3,
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \begin{vmatrix} 0 & -1 \\ 4 & 1 \end{vmatrix} = (0 \cdot 1) - (-1 \cdot 4) = 0 + 4 = 4,
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \begin{vmatrix} 0 & 5 \\ 4 & -2 \end{vmatrix} = (0 \cdot -2) - (5 \cdot 4) = 0 - 20 = -20.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Now, substitute these values back into the cofactor expansion:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \text{det} = 1 \cdot 3 - (-3) \cdot 4 + 3 \cdot (-20) = 3 + 12 - 60 = -45.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Therefore, the determinant of the matrix is \(\boxed{-45}\).<|im_end|>
