[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The repeating decimal \(0.\overline{6}\) can be expressed as the fraction \(\frac{2}{3}\). To confirm this, we can use algebraic manipulation. Let \(x = 0.\overline{6}\). Then \(10x = 6.\overline{6}\). Subtracting the original \(x\) from this equation, we get:
