[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus, the possible values of \(x\), \(y\), and \(z\) are \(x = 0\), \(y = 0\), and \(z = 0\). We need to find the sum of all possible values of \(\cos(2x - y - z)\):
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \cos(2 \cdot 0 - 0 - 0) = \cos(0) = 1.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Therefore, the sum of all possible values of \(\cos(2x - y - z)\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \boxed{1}.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]<|im_end|>
