[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 6. \( k = 6 \): \( k^k = 36 \)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 7. \( k = 7 \): \( k^k = 9 \) (same as k when starting from 1)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 8. \( k = 8 \): \( k^k = 27 \) (same as k starting from 2)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 9. \( k = 9 \): \( k^k = 64 \) (same as k starting from 3)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 10. \( k = 10 \): \( k^k = 100 \) (squared is too large to fit <1000)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus, the possible values for \( N \) are 1, 4, 27, 64, 9, 36, 900, 81, 26715600, and 15600. We can list these values as follows:
