[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find \( g(4) \), we need to determine the function \( g(x) \) given that \( f(x) = 2x - 3 \) and \( g(f(x)) = 5 - 4x \).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m First, we need to find the inverse of \( f(x) \) to express \( g(x) \) in terms of \( x \). The inverse function \( f^{-1}(x) \) is the function such that \( f(f^{-1}(x)) = x \) and \( f^{-1}(f(x)) = x \). For \( f(x) = 2x - 3 \), the inverse function \( f^{-1}(x) \) is found by solving \( y = 2x - 3 \) for \( x \):
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ y = 2x - 3 \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ y + 3 = 2x \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ x = \frac{y + 3}{2} \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Therefore, the inverse function is \( f^{-1}(x) = \frac{x + 3}{2} \). Now we know that if \( f(y) = x \), then \( f^{-1}(x) = y \). So, if \( f(x) = 2x - 3 \), then \( x = 2f^{-1}(y) + 3 \), where \( y = f(x) \).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The given function \( g(f(x)) = 5 - 4x \) has the inverse \( g(x) \). If we substitute \( f(x) \) into \( g(x) \), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ g(f(x)) = g(2x - 3) = 5 - 4x \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Comparing this with the given function \( g(f(x)) = 5 - 4x \), we see that \( g(x) = 5 - 4x \).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Finally, we need to find \( g(4) \):
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
