[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find the interval of all \( x \) such that both \( 2x \) and \( 3x \) are in the interval \( (1,2) \), we need to solve the following system of inequalities:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 1. \( 1 < 2x < 2 \)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2. \( 1 < 3x < 2 \)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m First, solve the left inequalities:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 1. \( 1 < 2x \)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    x > \frac{1}{2}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2. \( 2x < 2 \)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    x < 1
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Next, solve the right inequalities:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
