[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Since both inequalities must be satisfied simultaneously, the interval for \( x \) is the intersection of the intervals \( \left( \frac{1}{2}, 1 \right) \) and \( \left( -\infty, \frac{2}{3} \right) \). This intersection is \( \left( \frac{1}{2}, \frac{2}{3} \right) \).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Therefore, the interval of all \( x \) such that both \( 2x \) and \( 3x \) are in the interval \( (1,2) \) is \(\boxed{\left( \frac{1}{2}, \frac{2}{3} \right)}\).<|im_end|>
