[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To determine how many integers less than \(2019\) are \(20\)-pretty, we first interpret the problem in terms of the number of divisors of such numbers. A number has exactly \(k\) divisors if and only if it can be expressed in one of two principal factorized forms: \(d_1^{e_1} d_2^{e_2} \cdots d_m^{e_m}\), where \(d_i\) are distinct prime factors and \(e_1, e_2, \ldots, e_m\) are their respective exponents. For the number to have exactly \(k\) divisors, the exponents in its factorization must lie within the range from 1 to \(k\).
