[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To solve for \( t \) in the equation \( 3 \cdot 3^t + \sqrt{9 \cdot 9^t} = 18 \), we will break it down step by step.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m First, simplify the term inside the square root. Since \( 9 = 3^2 \), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \sqrt{9 \cdot 9^t} = \sqrt{(3^2) \cdot (3^t)^2} = \sqrt{3^{2+2t}} = \sqrt{3^{2(1+t)}} = 3^{1+t}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m So the equation becomes:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
