[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 3 \cdot 3^t = 18
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Dividing both sides by 3, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 3^t = 6
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To solve for \( t \), we take the logarithm of both sides. One common logarithm we can use is base 10. Taking the natural logarithm of both sides, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \ln(3^t) = \ln(6)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Using the property of logarithms that \(\ln(a^b) = b \ln(a)\), we have:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
