[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find the cost of transporting a 250 g control module, we need to convert the mass from grams to kilograms and then multiply by the constant cost per kilogram. Here are the steps:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 1. Convert the mass from grams to kilograms. There are 1000 grams in a kilogram, so we divide the mass in grams by 1000.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2. Use the given cost per kilogram to calculate the total cost.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m First, let's convert 250 grams to kilograms:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ 250 \text{ g} \div 1000 = 0.25 \text{ kg} \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Next, we use the cost per kilogram of $22,000 to calculate the cost:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ 0.25 \text{ kg} \times 22,000 \text{ dollars/kg} = 5,500 \text{ dollars} \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Therefore, the cost of transporting the 250 g control module is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ \boxed{5500} \]<|im_end|>
