[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - Original radius **\( r \)** = given, **\( r = 3\sqrt[3]{2} \)**  
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - Value **\( R \)**= radius of hemisphere because sphere + hemisphere (actually, hemisphere: sphere not included )
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - Volume of hemisphere = cylindrical volume
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2. **Initial volume of the spherical bubble:**
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - Given sphere volume: **\( V_{sphere} \) = \(\frac{4}{3}\pi r^3 = \frac{4}{3}\pi (3\sqrt[3]{2})^3\):
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    V_{sphere} = \frac{4}{3}\pi (3\sqrt[3]{2})^3 = \frac{4}{3}\pi (3\sqrt[3]{8}) = \frac{4}{3}\pi \cdot 3\cdot 2 \cdot \sqrt[3]{2} = 4\pi \cdot 6 \cdot \sqrt[3]{2} = 24\pi \sqrt[3]{2}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 3. **Volume of hemisphere:**
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - The volume of the hemisphere is \( V_{hemisphere} = \frac{1}{2} \left( \frac{4}{3}\pi R^3 \right) = \frac{2}{3}\pi R^3 = \frac{2}{3}\pi (3\sqrt[3]{2})^3
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - Given:  
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m      \text{V}_{hemisphere} = 3(3\sqrt[3]{2})^3 = 27\cdot2\cdot\sqrt[3]{8} = 27\cdot 2\cdot \sqrt[3]{2^3} = 54\sqrt[3]{4}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 4. **Set up the equation to solve for original water sphere radius formula:**
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - Using:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m      \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m      \frac{1}{2} \cdot 24\pi \sqrt[3]{\frac{V_{sphere}}{V_{hemisphere}}} = \frac{1}{2} \cdot 24\pi \cdot \sqrt[3]{\frac{24\pi \sqrt[3]{2}}{54\sqrt[3]{4}}} = r
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m      \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - Substituting and solving for r from the equation \( R^3 = r^3 \), we get 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    r = 12
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 5. **Conclusion:**
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \(\boxed{ 12 }\)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Therefore, the original radius of the spherical soap bubble is \( 12 \) cm.<|im_end|>
