[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find the largest integer value of \( x \) for which the inequality \( 5 - 4x > 17 \) holds true, we will follow these steps:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 1. **Isolate the term with \( x \) on one side of the inequality:**
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    5 - 4x > 17
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    Subtract 5 from both sides to isolate the term with \( x \):
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    -4x > 17 - 5
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    Simplify the right side:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    -4x > 12
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2. **Divide both sides by \(-4\):**
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    Remember that when we divide both sides of an inequality by a negative number, we must reverse the inequality sign:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    \[
