[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 3. **Counting the valid combinations:**
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - For each value of \(a\), there is exactly one valid combination \((b, c)\) except when \(a = 9\), in which case there are no valid pairs.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - Therefore, we have 7 valid combinations for each value of \(a \geq 1\), and 3 valid combinations for \(a = 1\).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 4. **Summing up the total count:**
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m    - There are 9 combinations for the hundreds digit (1 through 9).
