[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To solve the equation \(\sqrt{1 + \sqrt{2y-3}} = \sqrt{6}\), we start by eliminating the square roots on both sides. First, we square both sides of the equation to remove the outer square root:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m (\sqrt{1 + \sqrt{2y-3}})^2 = (\sqrt{6})^2
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 1 + \sqrt{2y-3} = 6
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Next, we isolate \(\sqrt{2y-3}\) by subtracting 1 from both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \sqrt{2y-3} = 5
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Now, we eliminate the outer square root by squaring both sides again:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m (\sqrt{2y-3})^2 = 5^2
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2y - 3 = 25
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m We solve for \(y\) by adding 3 to both sides and then dividing by 2:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2y = 28
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m y = 14
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus, the value of \(y\) is \(\boxed{14}\).<|im_end|>
