[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To determine the length of the segment of the number line whose endpoints satisfy \( |x - \sqrt[5]{16}| = 3 \), we first need to solve for \( x \) in terms of the given conditions. The equation \( |x - \sqrt[5]{16}| = 3 \) can be broken down into two separate absolute value equations:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m x - \sqrt[5]{16} = 3 \quad \text{or} \quad x - \sqrt[5]{16} = -3
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m We solve each equation separately.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 1. For the first equation:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m x - \sqrt[5]{16} = 3
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Add \(\sqrt[5]{16}\) to both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m x = 3 + \sqrt[5]{16}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2. For the second equation:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m x - \sqrt[5]{16} = -3
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Add \(\sqrt[5]{16}\) to both sides:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m x = -3 + \sqrt[5]{16}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus, the endpoints of the segment are \( x = 3 + \sqrt[5]{16} \) and \( x = -3 + \sqrt[5]{16} \). To find the length of the segment, we calculate the difference between these two points:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m (3 + \sqrt[5]{16}) - (-3 + \sqrt[5]{16}) = 3 + \sqrt[5]{16} + 3 - \sqrt[5]{16} = 6
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Therefore, the length of the segment is \(\boxed{6}\).<|im_end|>
