[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find the common ratio of the infinite geometric series \(\frac{5}{6} - \frac{4}{9} + \frac{32}{135} - \dots\), we need to determine the ratio between consecutive terms.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The first term \(a\) is \(\frac{5}{6}\).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The second term \(b\) is \(-\frac{4}{9}\).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The common ratio \(r\) is the ratio of the second term to the first term:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ r = \frac{b}{a} = \frac{-\frac{4}{9}}{\frac{5}{6}} = -\frac{4}{9} \times \frac{6}{5} = -\frac{24}{45} = -\frac{8}{15}. \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Therefore, the common ratio of the infinite geometric series is \(\boxed{-\frac{8}{15}}\).<|im_end|>
