[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m This inequality can be rewritten as:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m m^2 > 64
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Taking the square root of both sides, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m |m| > 8
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m This absolute value inequality means that \( m \) must be either greater than 8 or less than -8. Therefore, the possible values of \( m \) are:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
