[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m <|im_start|>assistant
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find the perimeter of the polygon formed when the points \( A(-6,6) \), \( B(9,6) \), and \( C(9,-2) \) are graphed and connected with straight lines, we first need to determine the lengths of the sides of this triangle.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The distance formula between two points \((x_1, y_1)\) and \((x_2, y_2)\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m d = \sqrt{(x_2 - x_1)^2 + (y_2 - y_1)^2}
