[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find the magnitude of the projection of vector \(\mathbf{v}\) onto vector \(\mathbf{w}\), we start with the given information that the dot product \(\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w} = -3\) and the magnitude of \(\mathbf{w}\), \(\|\mathbf{w}\| = 5\).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The formula for the projection of \(\mathbf{v}\) onto \(\mathbf{w}\) is given by:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v} = \frac{\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w}}{\|\mathbf{w}\|} \mathbf{w}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The magnitude of this projection is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \left\| \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v} \right\| = \left| \frac{\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w}}{\|\mathbf{w}\|} \mathbf{w} \right|
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Since \(\mathbf{w}\) is a unit vector, \(\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w}\) is the scalar triple product and equals the product of the magnitudes of \(\mathbf{v}\) and \(\mathbf{w}\), which is \(5^2 = 25\). Therefore, the magnitude of the projection of \(\mathbf{v}\) onto \(\mathbf{w}\) simplifies to:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \left\| \operatorname{proj}_{\mathbf{w}} \mathbf{v} \right\| = \left| \frac{25}{5} \mathbf{v} \right| = 5 \times 25 = 125
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus, the magnitude of the projection of \(\mathbf{v}\) onto \(\mathbf{w}\) is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \boxed{125}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]<|im_end|>
