[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To determine the units digit of \(\frac{2^{1993} + 3^{1993}}{5}\), we start by examining the units digits of the powers of 2 and 3 and their combinations modulo 5.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m First, we find the pattern of the units digits of \(2^n\) modulo 5:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \begin{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2^1 &\equiv 2 \pmod{5}, \\
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2^2 &\equiv 4 \pmod{5}, \\
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2^3 &\equiv 8 \equiv 3 \pmod{5}, \\
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 2^4 &\equiv 16 \equiv 1 \pmod{5}.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \end{align*}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The units digits repeat every 4 terms: 2, 4, 3, 1. Therefore, to find the units digit of \(2^{1993}\), we need to determine the remainder when 1993 is divided by 4:
