[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m pq + qr + rp = 8
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m pqr = -2
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m We need to find \(\frac{1}{p^2} + \frac{1}{q^2} + \frac{1}{r^2}\). This expression can be rewritten using the square of a difference:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \frac{1}{p^2} + \frac{1}{q^2} + \frac{1}{r^2} = \frac{q^2r^2 + p^2r^2 + p^2q^2}{p^2q^2r^2} = \frac{(q^2r^2 + p^2r^2 + p^2q^2) - 2(pqr + pq + qr)}{p^2q^2r^2}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m First, we calculate the numerator \(q^2r^2 + p^2r^2 + p^2q^2 - 2(pqr + pq + qr)\). Since \(p + q + r = 9\) and \(pqr = -2\), we can use the identity for the sum of squares:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m q^2r^2 + p^2r^2 + p^2q^2 - 2(pqr + pq + qr) = (qr)(rp - pq) + (qr)(rp + pq) + (pr)(pq) - 2(pqr + pq + qr)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m = q^2r^2 + p^2r^2 + p^2q^2 - 2 \cdot 2(q + p + r) = q^2r^2 + p^2r^2 + p^2q^2 - 4(q + p + r)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Substituting the known values:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m = 8 + 9p + 9q - 8 = 9(p + q + r)
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Therefore, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \frac{1}{p^2} + \frac{1}{q^2} + \frac{1}{r^2} = \frac{9(p + q + r)}{p^2q^2r^2} = \frac{9 \cdot 9}{(-2)^2} = \frac{81}{4}
