[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The product of the roots taken one at a time is equal to the negation of the constant term \(b\) divided by the leading coefficient (which is 1 in this case). Therefore, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m (1 + i \sqrt{3})(1 - i \sqrt{3})(-2) = b
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Simplifying the left side, we get:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m (1 + i \sqrt{3})(1 - i \sqrt{3}) = 1^2 - (i \sqrt{3})^2 = 1 - (-3) = 1 + 3 = 4
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Thus, we have:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 4(-2) = -8 \implies b = -8
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Therefore, \(a + b = -2 - 8 = -10\). The final answer is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \boxed{-10}
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \]<|im_end|>
