[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m To find the total area of the shaded regions, we need to calculate the area of the larger circle and subtract the area of the smaller circle (since the shaded region is the difference between the areas of two circles).
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m First, we find the radius of the larger circle. Since the area of a circle is given by the formula \( \pi r^2 \), we can use the area of the larger circle to find its radius.
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The area of the larger circle is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ 64\pi \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The area of the larger circle is also given by:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ \pi r_{\text{large}}^2 = 64\pi \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m By solving for \( r_{\text{large}} \), we get:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ r_{\text{large}}^2 = 64 \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ r_{\text{large}} = \sqrt{64} = 8 \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The area of the larger circle is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ \pi r_{\text{large}}^2 = 64\pi \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The area of the smaller circle is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ \pi r_{\text{small}}^2 \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m We already know the area of the smaller circle:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ \pi r_{\text{small}}^2 = \pi \cdot 4^2 = 16\pi \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m The shaded area is the difference between the area of the larger circle and the area of the smaller circle:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ \pi r_{\text{large}}^2 - \pi r_{\text{small}}^2 = 64\pi - 16\pi = 48\pi \]
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m 
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m Therefore, the total area of the shaded regions is:
[36m(main_task pid=3409)[0m \[ \boxed{48\pi} \]<|im_end|>
